            <ArticleTitle>Coeliac plexus block and cephalic spread of injectate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>48-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Extensive cephalic spread of solution occurred in three out of seven cases studied during coeliac plexus blockade. Spread on to cardiac nerves and plexus may be a factor in hypotension following this procedure. Incremental dosage and careful screening is recommended.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
